==English==

===Etymology===
from Latin [[dis-]] (apart) + [[satis]] (enough) + [[facere]] (to make).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/dɪsˈsætəsˌfaɪd/}}, {{SAMPA|/dIs"s{t@s%faId/}}
* {{audio|en-us-dissatisfied.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Feeling or displaying disappointment or a lack of contentment
# Not [[satisfied]] (with the [[quality]] of something)

